Your glossary and your team disagree: the glossary says an order exists only once the customer submits at checkout, but the team also uses "order" for a cart with items that was never submitted. Those are two different things sharing one name, so the term needs settling before the design does.

I checked `/workspace` and it's an empty scaffold with no `GLOSSARY.md`, no ADRs and no checkout code. So nothing in code constrains the terms yet, and I've written nothing.

Here is the first round of questions; a "yes" accepts my recommendation.

❓ **Q1 - What does "Order" mean?** Dana adds two items on Monday and never checks out. On Tuesday someone asks "how many orders did we get yesterday?" Does Dana count? The options are:
- **(a)** Order means submitted only, and Dana's thing is a **Cart**.
- **(b)** Order covers both, split into "Draft Order" and "Placed Order".
- **(c)** Something else.

➡️ (a). Keep the glossary definition as is, call the unsubmitted thing a **Cart**, and list "order" under Cart as a term to avoid. Option (b) means every use of "order" needs a qualifier, and people will drop it.

---

❓ **Q2 - What exactly is "submit"?** Sam clicks "Place order" and the card is declined. Does an Order exist at that moment? Either an Order exists from the click, in an awaiting-payment state, or nothing is an Order until payment succeeds and Sam is still holding a Cart.

➡️ An Order exists from the click, whatever the payment outcome. That matches the glossary wording ("what the customer submits"), gives support something to look up when Sam calls, and makes payment retries attach to one stable thing.

---

❓ **Q3 - What is in scope for the redesign?** I'm assuming it covers the path from a Cart with items to a submitted Order: address, delivery, payment, review and submit. Catalogue and browsing, and everything after submission (fulfilment, returns), would be out except where checkout hands off to them.

➡️ Yes, that scope. If a specific pain is driving the redesign (abandonment, payment failures, guest checkout), tell me, because it changes which questions matter most.

---

❓ **Q4 - Where does the glossary live?** There's no glossary file in this repo, so the one you quoted lives somewhere else.

➡️ Once Q1 is settled, I create `GLOSSARY.md` at the repo root, seeded with your existing Order definition plus whatever we resolve, and it becomes the source of truth for this work. If the canonical one lives elsewhere, such as a wiki, point me to it and I'll mirror it rather than fork it.

---

Later questions depend on these answers: whether there is a third concept between Cart and Order (a checkout in progress), whether an Order is a snapshot of the Cart, what happens to the Cart after submission, and whether an empty cart is a Cart at all.

