❓ **Q4** - **What is a "team"?**: Is a team simply the set of Users in an Account that is on a team plan, or a subgroup inside an Account (say, Engineering and Sales at one company)? Shall we say there is no separate Team entity, so "team plan" is just a Plan an Account is on, and "team" is not a glossary term?

➡️ Yes. Subgroups are a separate feature with their own permission questions. If "Team" sits in the vocabulary next to "Account", you recreate the ambiguity you are fixing now.

---

❓ **Q5** - **What does a team plan charge for?**: Shall the team plan be priced per **Seat**, so the Account pays for each User it has, rather than a flat price with a cap on Users?

➡️ Yes, assuming your pricing isn't already fixed. Per-seat is the norm buyers expect, and it forces us to define "Seat" precisely next round (whether pending invitations or deactivated Users count). If pricing is already decided as flat tiers, say so and we skip Seat.

